00:20:34,110 --> 00:20:35,600
 Their radio may have gone out.

244
00:20:35,940 --> 00:20:39,710
 That's what we suppose, Lieutenant. Radios all at once.

245
00:20:39,710 --> 00:20:43,760
 We'll contact our station. Let us know of any new developments.

246
00:20:43,900 --> 00:20:44,880
 Yes, Lieutenant. Thanks.

247
00:20:46,110 --> 00:20:49,820
 Four hours. If you go into hyperspace, we could miss them.

248
00:20:50,320 --> 00:20:54,020
 If you go on in normal space, it'll take us at least seven hours to catch them.

249
00:20:54,350 --> 00:20:56,630
 That is, if you're right on guessing the direction they took.

250
00:20:57,210 --> 00:20:59,660
 Otherwise, with every second that goes by,

251
00:20:59,760 --> 00:21:03,500
 their chances of disappearing into a corner of the galaxy increases exponentially.

252
00:21:03,960 --> 00:21:06,650
 I think I can guess the direction they've taken.

253
00:21:07,150 --> 00:21:10,040
 Yes, so can I. And it's the same direction.

254
00:21:11,200 --> 00:21:15,060
 If we calculate our hyperspace configuration to within a fraction of a second,

255
00:21:15,060 --> 00:21:16,350
 And we just might...

256
00:21:16,350 --> 00:21:17,580
 Let's try it, Piero.

257
00:21:17,940 --> 00:21:20,280
 And you, how about a brief introduction to hyperspace?

258
00:21:20,420 --> 00:21:21,040
 Think that'll be all right?

259
00:21:21,040 --> 00:21:22,400
 Oh, don't ask me twice!

260
00:21:22,700 --> 00:21:25,000
 With an experience like that, do you think I wouldn't miss a thing like that?

261
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:26,020
 You go ahead, I'm not scared.

262
00:21:26,300 --> 00:21:27,720
 Ready? Let's go.

263
00:21:28,160 --> 00:21:29,360
 Antigravitation shield.

264
00:21:38,320 --> 00:21:47,280
 The train.

265
00:21:57,750 --> 00:22:01,600
 Using magnetic destroyers.

266
00:22:02,060 --> 00:22:06,210
 It's hard to get close to the magnetic protection field wasn't operating.

267
00:22:06,480 --> 00:22:07,670
 See if there's any damage.

268
00:22:08,020 --> 00:22:09,190
 I'll contact Omega.

269
00:22:09,690 --> 00:22:10,990
 Central computer, okay.

270
00:22:11,800 --> 00:22:12,930
 Propulsion, okay.

271
00:22:14,330 --> 00:22:15,210
 Gravitation, okay.

272
00:22:15,630 --> 00:22:16,970
 Airtight seals, okay.

273
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:24,600
 Guidance system, okay. Radar screen, not okay. There is a slight leak in the hermetic ceiling.

274
00:22:26,800 --> 00:22:29,920
 This is Omega Control. Come in, Lieutenant Piero.

275
00:22:30,660 --> 00:22:35,100
 This is Lieutenant Piero. We've managed to find that mineral train.

276
00:22:35,980 --> 00:22:40,820
 Diverted from mineral base HX-41, we've been hit by a mine and able to give chase.

277
00:22:41,310 --> 00:22:42,310
 Do we open fire?

278
00:22:43,130 --> 00:22:48,170
 This is the commander. Do not fire, Piero. Train must be recovered. It's vital.

279
00:22:48,170 --> 00:22:51,320
 I'll send a squadron to intercept. Can you make it back?

280
00:22:52,510 --> 00:22:55,030
 We'll see, commander. Pressure in the cabin?

281
00:22:55,360 --> 00:22:58,940
 Pressure at maximum. It will hold for a while, not long.

282
00:22:59,320 --> 00:23:00,580
 Circular periscoping position.

283
00:23:00,720 --> 00:23:01,280
 Piero, look!

284
00:23:04,620 --> 00:23:10,300
 Too bad Metro isn't here. He could go out there and repair it.

285
00:23:10,360 --> 00:23:11,300
 I guess I'll have to try.

286
00:23:12,030 --> 00:23:15,230
 Now you stay at the control. Remain in radio contact.

287
00:23:29,220 --> 00:23:32,380
 Terrific sight. I think I can repair the damage.

288
00:23:32,840 --> 00:23:35,390
 Loud and clear, Piero. Only hurry, there isn't much time.

289
00:23:35,750 --> 00:23:37,580
 I've almost finished the repair job.

290
00:23:38,160 --> 00:23:40,500
 Broken metal shielding doesn't want to come off.

291
00:23:41,940 --> 00:23:45,290
 Oh, Piero, please, it's okay. It will hold like that.

292
00:24:00,940 --> 00:24:02,280
 He's lost in space.

293
00:24:02,880 --> 00:24:04,610
 Oh my goodness, what can we do?

294
00:24:04,610 --> 00:24:08,360
 The only thing you can do is let me concentrate.

295
00:24:08,360 --> 00:24:10,280
 Piero, where are you?

296
00:24:10,280 --> 00:24:12,110
 Piero, you must hear me.

297
00:24:12,110 --> 00:24:14,610
 Piero, where are you?

298
00:24:14,610 --> 00:24:19,090
 Piero, you hear me?

299
00:24:19,090 --> 00:24:21,830
 Piero, speak to me.

300
00:24:21,830 --> 00:24:31,730
 Piero, you're talking to me, Piero.

301
00:24:31,730 --> 00:24:33,840
 It's the only way I can find you.

302
00:24:33,840 --> 00:24:44,220
 Keep it tight, speak to me.

303
00:24:44,220 --> 00:24:48,240
 Go on, don't stop talking.

304
00:24:48,240 --> 00:24:50,650
 See the ship, I can see you.

305
00:24:50,650 --> 00:24:52,550
 Wait a minute, Piero, I'll turn the ship

306
00:24:52,550 --> 00:24:55,070
 so you can enter by the rear deck.

307
00:24:55,070 --> 00:24:57,490
 That old crate never looks so cut.

308
00:24:57,490 --> 00:25:02,390
 You'll be all right, Piero, it's over now.

309
00:25:02,390 --> 00:25:04,170
 You've made up your mind.

310
00:25:04,170 --> 00:25:11,920
 Oh, yes, Madam President. I'm going to return to Earth. Sorry, my companions want to stay here, but I'll admit things go a bit too quickly for me here.

311
00:25:11,970 --> 00:25:13,740
 But on Earth, things have changed, too.

312
00:25:13,840 --> 00:25:20,240
 No doubt, no doubt. But Earth is my home. I want to see it. There are some things that certainly couldn't have changed.

313
00:25:21,980 --> 00:25:25,080
 No word on the Space Jack train. Have to take action.

314
00:25:25,220 --> 00:25:26,860
 I'd be glad to, but action against whom?

315
00:25:27,280 --> 00:25:28,200
 One guess.

316
00:25:28,820 --> 00:25:30,920
 Suspicion of guilt is not enough, and you know it.

317
00:25:31,280 --> 00:25:34,070
 Very well. I am convening a summit meeting. We'll see.

318
00:25:34,530 --> 00:25:36,460
 Is this train so important?

319
00:25:36,460 --> 00:25:40,470
 Yes, it is, but it's top secret, in the hands of a troublemaker.

320
00:25:40,470 --> 00:25:43,100
 Well, there are some curious goings on there.

321
00:25:43,100 --> 00:25:48,230
 Right. Too many. I wonder if it's who I think it is.

322
00:25:48,230 --> 00:25:54,440
 One day we'll come to visit you.

323
00:25:54,440 --> 00:25:55,240
 On Earth!

324
00:25:55,240 --> 00:25:56,040
 There's a promise.

325
00:25:56,040 --> 00:25:59,840
 Oh, my goodness.

326
00:25:59,840 --> 00:26:20,770
 We're glad you came.

327
00:26:20,770 --> 00:26:40,670
 So, Wander, come take your place.

